# VibeCheck environment variables: a template.
#
# How to use: copy this file to a new file called `.env` in this same folder,
# then fill in the real values. `.env` is ignored by git, so your values stay
# on your PC. Never put real values in this example file.
#
# Why the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix: Expo only copies variables that start with
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ into the app. That means these values end up inside the app on
# people's phones, so only put values here that are safe to be public.
# The Supabase URL and "anon" key are public by design (the database's
# row-level security rules protect the data). The Supabase SERVICE ROLE key is
# NOT safe and must never go in this file, in .env, or in git.
#
# These are filled in during task VC-B02 (Supabase setup). The app doesn't read
# them yet.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
